          "en": "The establishment of this resort has the following objectives: - to conserve the cultural heritage in the fields of archaeology, ethnology and history and to enhance the value of the resort and protect it still further; - to conserve the cultural landscape and develop the tourism area; - to protect the natural environment in the area according to the actual geographical situation.\nAll development of the protected resort shall be monitored in compliance with the zoning plans and the management arrangements of the area according to the category of the protected zone.\nArticle 4.- The Koh Ker protected resort shall be divided into 3 (three) separate zones and shall receive different levels of protection.\n1- The core zone: a zone containing the large temple called zone K, and Rahal called zone B.\nBoth (two) zones shall be determined as follows: - Zone K: the area to be determined within the perimeter of the boundary line of the points; - Zone B: the area to be determined within the perimeter of the boundary line of the points.\nThis core zone has a total area of 92 hectares 62 ares (ninety-two hectares and sixty-two ares).\nZones K and B are protected resorts and shall receive the highest level of protection.\n2- The support zone: an archaeological park zone, comprising one small temple and numerous archaeological remains left behind as traces, foundations or shallow or deep ground structures in the fields, forests and so on, which archaeologists have discovered and which have not yet been excavated.\nThis zone has an area of 3,507 hectares 63 ares (three thousand five hundred and seven hectares and sixty-three ares).\nThis zone is located outside the perimeter of zones K and B, that is, outside the core zone, and lies within the perimeter of the boundary line of the points; this zone contains archaeological remains that require protection and the prevention of land use and inappropriate development.\n3- The buffer zone: an economic and social development zone, maintaining the livelihood, occupations and businesses according to customs and traditions, as well as the residence of the citizens in the area. This zone is located outside the perimeter with coordinates at a distance of 1,500 metres (one thousand five hundred metres). This zone is a target for the conservation of cultural and natural heritage through the arrangement of measures to promote sustainable development and environmental impact assessment.\nThe map determining the zones of the Koh Ker temple resort is annexed to this Royal Decree.\nManagement, maintenance and protection: the conservation of each zone shall be managed, maintained and protected in accordance with the specific directions and levels of importance in the fields of archaeology, ethnology, history, environment and natural assets, respecting the ownership rights of the citizens living in the entire area as regards their livelihood, and enhancing the value of the protected resort.\nThe policy of the Supreme Council for National Culture shall be implemented in order to ensure management, maintenance and protection by determining the ownership and responsibility of the competent institutions, with the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts directly responsible, on the basis of Article 5 of the Law on the Protection of Cultural Heritage promulgated by Royal Kram No. NS/RKM/0196/26 dated 25 January 1996. The modalities and procedures for the management, maintenance and protection of the Koh Ker temple resort under the above articles, and every activity of each zone of the Koh Ker protected resort, may be reviewed and amended in part on the basis of every result of research by archaeologists and the actual situation, in order to ensure economic and social development, conservation and sustainable management as provided in Article 4 of this Royal Decree. - Any change of zone and every activity relating to the Koh Ker temple resort shall be determined by Royal Decree."
